# class Mine extends RegExp { static get [Symbol.species]() { return Other } }; function Other() { }; "a,b".split(new Mine(","))
# split asks the pattern for Symbol.split. What that answers comes back to where the pattern stands, so an object nobody knows stands beside the pattern, and the pattern, which is kept, has escaped.
# RegExp.prototype[Symbol.split] still reads `constructor` from the pattern and Symbol.species from that, however late either is found, and constructs the answer.
